From Zero to Hero: Building a CI/CD Pipeline from Scratch (Real-World Edition)

Ever wondered how modern teams deliver features to production with speed and confidence?

It all starts with a solid CI/CD (Continuous Integration/Continuous Deployment) pipeline! Whether you're a beginner or looking to level up your DevOps game, here’s a simple roadmap to building your pipeline: 👇

🔁 Typical CI/CD Workflow

1️⃣ Code Commit
 → Triggers CI pipeline automatically
2️⃣ Build Stage
 → Compile (Java/Node/Go)
 → Run Unit Tests
 → Lint, Format, Scan code
3️⃣ Image Build & Push
 → Docker/Buildah/Kaniko builds container
 → Push to Harbor/ECR
 → Tag with commit hash/version
4️⃣ Manifest Update
 → Helm chart or K8s YAML updated with new image tag
 → Pushed to Git (GitOps trigger)
5️⃣ Deployment (CD)
 → ArgoCD auto-syncs repo with Kubernetes
 → Deploys the new image
 → Monitors rollout & health checks

🔐 Add-ons for Production:
✅ Secrets Management → External Secrets + AWS SM
 ✅ Notifications → Slack/Webhook Alerts
 ✅ Rollbacks → ArgoCD Rollback or Helm history
 ✅ Canary / Blue-Green → Progressive delivery with Argo Rollouts or Istio
 ✅ Infra as Code → Terraform for provisioning EKS

🧠 Pro Tip:
Start simple, grow modular.
 Even a basic CI/CD with Git + Actions + K8s + Helm can power large-scale production apps
